            <note corresp="#d971-f3" n="3" xml:id="d971-f3-content">
                <p>Dated July 18, <ref target="#pg1426">p. 1426</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d971-f4" n="4" xml:id="d971-f4-content">
                <p>The U.S. Delegation transmitted an additional report on this conversation in
                    telegram Secto 658, July 19. It read as
                    follows: “During conversation with Tran Van
                        Do (Secto 656), Bonsal asked Do purpose Tran Van Huu‘s
                    visit to Geneva last week. Do said
                        Huu had seen Pham Van Dong to sound out possibilities of
                    coalition government. When Bonsal
                    expressed surprise, Do said Huu would do anything to get into power.
                        Do said he realized impossibility
                    coalition government from experience in 1946. Even one Viet Minh in coalition
                    would lead to disaster.” (396.1 GE/7–1954)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
